# tlo: dziady
# rozdzial: Chapter Twenty
# tytul: The Last Night
On the second of November Zapadlina woke in a mist so thick that the well could not be seen from the threshold. No one went to the woods for brushwood, nor down to the lake with the washing. From early morning the women scrubbed benches and tables, and the men chopped firewood right up against the cottage walls, so as not to stray more than two steps from the door. On the palings facing the forest a lichen was greying—dry and brittle, though on everything else the mist settled in beads of water.
{ przysiega_ksiedzu:
    Before noon the priest rode over from Bukowiec with an aspergillum and a pail of holy water, to bless the fences. At Jaromir’s cottage he reined in his horse.
    “Are you keeping what you swore on the rosary?” he asked. # pokaz: ksiadz
    { cialo_kopii == spalone || cialo_kopii == pod_mlodnikiem:
        Jaromir said nothing. The priest turned his horse about; their fence he left unsprinkled.
    - else:
        “I am,” Jaromir answered. The priest sprinkled the fence twice over.
    }
}
On every windowsill stood a bowl of porridge and a cup of water. In every house one more place was left laid at the table—for those who come back on this night. # dalej
{ marysia_odzyskana:
    Hanka sat Marysia down by the stove and never let her out of her sight.
- else:
    Hanka laid two extra places: one for the forefathers, and a second, small one, with the wooden spoon Jaromir had whittled the winter before. No one said a word.
}
