# tlo: swita
They came before midnight.
First a hush fell—so deep that Jaromir could hear the embers crackling in the stove inside. Then the mist parted, and along the road from the forest the retinue entered the village.
They walked slowly, without the faintest sound. From the front ranks came a breath of silt and damp, from the rear—of sweet, rotten wood. The one-eyed beggar woman in her rags, leaning on a staff. Lady Midnight, tall, flat as a shadow on a wall{ polnocnica == policzyla_mak:, with the poppy seeds in her clenched fist}. Rusalki in wet shifts, called up from the silt out of their season—water dripped from their hair, and among them walked Kaśka, the Wójciks’ daughter{ ratunek_franka == krzyzem:, and Bartek, the miller’s son, with waterweed round his neck}. Mamunas with their washing paddles. The rye mother, hunched, with ears of grain in her hair{ not wilk_przy_jaromirze: and a red clog in her hand}. Wisplings, bobbing above their heads like lanterns.{ los_figurki == figurka_u_stwora: The creature from the marshes, stooped, the figurine pressed to its breast the way a mother holds a child.}{ poludnica_uklon: Lady Midday in her white shift; as she passed, she bowed to Jaromir—just as she had that time on the stubble field.} The children under the oak, hand in hand. Not one of them cast a shadow. # pokaz: swita, dzieci # dalej
{ not marysia_odzyskana:
    Among them was one who held no one’s hand. Barefoot, in a little white shift, with no ribbon in her hair. She walked more slowly than the others and kept looking round at the cottages, as if searching for the way home. Hanka saw her through the window. She did not cry out. She only clasped the Candlemas candle to her breast, so tightly that the wax ran down over her fingers, and yet the flame did not waver. # pokaz: marysia
}
The dead of Zapadlina walked among them too. Old Wójcik{ pochowek_wojcika == pochowany_za_murem || trzy_noce == rozkopany_grob:—his face turned towards the ground, though he walked upright}.{ trzy_noce == czuwanie_przy_kolysce: Mrs Wójcik, her hands folded on her breast{ korale_kaski == oddane: and her daughter’s beads beneath her headscarf}.} Grandmother Marianna. And ahead of them all—Grandfather Maciek, with an axe in his belt and a bundle on his shoulder, just as he had been seventy years before, when he first came down into Zapadlina. As he passed the cottage, he looked at his grandson and nodded to him. # pokaz: umarli
Last of all, stooping so as not to catch his antlers on the sky, came the Lord of the Forest. Each of his strides was as long as a field strip. Moss sprang up wherever he trod, and at once turned grey with hoarfrost. # pokaz: leszy
He halted before Jaromir’s cottage. The retinue stopped behind him. # dalej
