= calun_nad_jeziorem
The mamunas stepped out of the ranks. The eldest raised a small, wet cloth on her outstretched hands, showed it to Jaromir and, without a word, set off with the others towards the lake.
“Go,” said the Lord of the Forest, without turning his head. “I shall wait. The night is long.” # dalej
# tlo: calun_noc
On the flat stones on the far side of the lake the mamunas spread the cloth out and smoothed it with their palms. It was still wet, though two months had passed since August. Just the size of a child. The lake lay black and smooth, and not a sound carried from the village. # pokaz: mamuny
“Marysia,” said the eldest over the shroud, tenderly, and slapped her paddle against the stone. “Marysia.”
{
- dar_pominiety:
