- else:
    “It’s not us as chooses,” she croaked. “We wash what the water brings us, and now the water’s bringing children from your village.”
}
“By dawn it’ll be dry,” she said. “Then nobody can wash the name out, not even us. While it’s wet, it still can be done.” She smiled with black gums. “Only nothing comes off the cloth without a price.” # pokaz: calun
# pytanie: What will Jaromir do?
*   [Tear the shroud from them himself.]
    ~ cena_caluna = cena_zdrowie
    He waded in up to his knees and snatched the shroud off the stone. The mamunas fell upon him—cold, wet hands twined about his arms and calves, and the paddles came down on his back like flails on a threshing floor. He did not let go. When he clambered out onto the bank, the cloth was streaming in his fists, and from the water behind him the giggling went on for a long while. # pokaz: wyrwany
    The name was washed away. But the chill of the lake stayed in him: from the knees down his legs were as cold as stones from the lake bed, and nothing ever warmed them again—neither the stove nor a sheepskin coat. He never took up a scythe again.
*   [Call Antek.]
    ~ cena_caluna = cena_antek
    “Antek!” Jaromir shouted towards the village. Antek, who had not slept that night, came running to the lake before the echo had died away over the water. He asked nothing. He walked in among the mamunas as though he were walking into the smithy, and tore the shroud from the stone—the shroud of the little girl he had held at the font. # pokaz: antek
    The eldest swung her paddle. In the stillness came a crack like a branch snapping. Antek did not cry out. He came out onto the bank with the shroud in his left hand, while his right hung twisted at the elbow in a way no arm ever bends. The smith looked at it afterwards and only shook his head. Antek never went back to the smithy.
*   { wilk_przy_jaromirze && znak_rozpoznania != po_wilku } [Call the white wolf.]
    ~ cena_caluna = cena_franek
    ~ zapiski += tropy_6
    “Franek!” Jaromir called towards the village, not even knowing whether the wolf would hear. The name, the heaviest of all words, travelled out over the water.
    The wolf heard. A white shadow streaked along the shore, burst in among the mamunas and tore the shroud to shreds with his teeth. They let out a piercing wail and flung themselves on him all at once. The water by the stones seethed like a washing cauldron—and then lay smooth again. # pokaz: wilk
    At the water’s edge, among the reeds, lay a white body, heavy with water. Antek, who had come running at the howl, knelt beside it and laid his hand on the ring of worn fur round the foreleg. “It’s him,” was all he said. “I told you.”{ wilk_pod_debem == opowiedzial_o_antku: Jaromir recalled the words spoken under the oak: with your memories in his head he will not live long.}
*   { uklad_z_mamunami == dar_swietojanski && not dar_pominiety } [Remind them of the bargain and extend it to his daughter.]
    ~ cena_caluna = cena_umowa
    “I promised you a gift for as long as I live,” said Jaromir. “So be it: for as long as she lives. When I am gone, she will bring it herself.”
    The eldest studied him without moving. Then she set down her paddle. “Agreed,” she croaked. “But she’ll have to remember too. Every year. To the end.”
    When Jaromir reached for the shroud, the cloth melted away in the water like foam. # pokaz: piana
    { przysiega_ksiedzu:
        The oath he had sworn in Bukowiec—to have done with gifts for what dwells in the water—he broke on the very night the priest had blessed his fence.
    }
