# tlo: granica
“You shall have your boundary,” said Jaromir. “But not from me alone.”
He went round the whole village and beneath every window called the householders by name. Antek was the first to come out{ cena_caluna == cena_antek:, his right sleeve tucked into his belt}. Then the smith, and Szymon{ noc_ognia == ratowal_kapliczke:, his face swathed in a cloth and his hands bound in rags}. Józek led old Staś by the hand, so aged now that he could barely see. His father, {noga_ojca == strzaskana:on crutches|leaning on a stick}, and his mother, muffled in a sheepskin. Last of all Hanka{ marysia_odzyskana:, with Marysia wrapped in her shawl}. They followed him through the mist with Candlemas candles that would not burn{ not marysia_odzyskana:—only Hanka’s was alight}, straight through the midst of the retinue. Rusalki and mamunas drew aside before them like water before the prow of a boat. # pokaz: ludzie
The stump of the Old Oak stood at the edge of the forest, black and overgrown with tinder fungus. The Lord of the Forest took his stand on the far side of it. # pokaz: leszy # dalej
{ zastaw_u_leszego == zastaw_siekiera:
    The Lord of the Forest reached into the darkness behind his back and handed Jaromir his grandfather’s axe. The haft was damp with the sap of the root that had held it.
- else:
    The Lord of the Forest looked at the grandfather’s axe in Jaromir’s hands.
}
“{chata_macka == przy_lesie:With this iron your grandfather crossed the boundary|With this iron your kin hewed my forest},” he said. “That one, the first, came to me without iron. You will leave yours behind.”
~ ekwipunek -= siekiera
Jaromir drove the axe into the stump until the wood groaned. The haft was heavy and cold, and his hands shook so badly that he had to strike twice. # pokaz: siekiera
