    ~ zoladz_zasadzony = true
    Then he knelt and scraped out a hollow in the frozen earth with his fingers, until his nails broke. Into it he laid the acorn he had kept since his boyhood—still warm. When he covered it over with clods, a pale shoot pushed up from beneath them—in November, in the frost. # pokaz: kielek
}
{ dlug_jagny:
- oddana_wstazka:
    Jagna stepped out of the mist and wound Marysia’s red ribbon round the haft of the axe. “Told you it’d come in handy,” she muttered. # pokaz: wstazka
- oddany_drewniak:
    Jagna stepped out of the mist and set the red clog down by the stump. “Wood to wood,” she muttered. # pokaz: drewniak
}
“We will go no further,” said Jaromir. His breath burst from his mouth in a cloud. Behind him they all repeated it, raggedly, hoarsely.{ pani_w_zbozu_noc == za_spiewem: Hanka only moved her lips.} “A word for a word.” # dalej
{ zoladz_zasadzony:
    The Lord of the Forest did not look at the axe. He looked at the shoot. He bent over it so low that his antlers snagged on the mist, and touched it with one finger—gently, the way one touches a foal that has only just found its legs.
    “That one, the first, gave me a word,” he said quietly. “And for it I took a child a generation, for a word weighs nothing, and the Oak was mine, not yours.” He straightened up. “This one is yours. It grew from my Oak, and it was planted by a hand that kept it safe a whole life long. Until now you have only ever given me what was yours. You have given me back what is mine. While this oak grows, I will take no children from you. You—no further than this iron. The shrines you will set up again. Every one of them. And you will keep watch over the word and the tree to the end of your days. Every All Souls’—here.”
    Hanka seized Jaromir’s hand.{ marysia_odzyskana: Marysia slept on in the shawl, not knowing that she had just been ransomed from the forest—she and every child still to be born in Zapadlina.}
- else:
    The Lord of the Forest looked at the axe in the stump. Then he nodded.
    “A word for a word,” he said. “You—no further than this iron. I—one child a generation, on Midsummer Night. And I will give it back before it forgets its home. The shrines you will set up again. Every one of them.” He bent down over Jaromir. “And you will keep the word as long as you live. Every All Souls’—here.”
}
{ przysiega_ksiedzu:
    Jaromir thought of the rosary and of the oath sworn in Bukowiec. He had just broken it{ cena_caluna == cena_umowa || cialo_kopii == spalone || cialo_kopii == pod_mlodnikiem: for the second time}—and he knew he would break it yet again.
}
The Lord of the Forest turned and went back into the forest. His servants followed him in, one behind another, and the mist closed over the last of them.{ not zoladz_zasadzony || marysia_odzyskana: The dead did not go with him; they dispersed along the road to Beech Ridge, each towards their own rest.}{ wilk_zywy() && not wilk_przy_mnie(): The white wolf walked just ahead of the Lord of the Forest.}{ wilk_przy_mnie(): The white wolf lingered a moment longer by Jaromir’s leg, then ran after them and did not look back.}
